<title>HUNGARY: NOVOTRADE SWINGS TO AFTER-TAX PROFIT IN '96.</title>
<headline>NOVOTRADE SWINGS TO AFTER-TAX PROFIT IN '96.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					     1996		   1995</p>
<p>    Group operating loss	     72.4	  vs     50.2</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit	    410.7	  vs     17.8</p>
<p>    Group after-tax result	  381.0 profit vs     10.9 loss</p>
<p>    Group net sales		 6,878.9	  vs  3,798.4</p>
<p>     Group foreign sales	  1,381.9	  vs  1,305.7</p>
<p>     Group domestic sales	 5,047.0	  vs  2,492.6</p>
<p>    Other revenues		    697.8	  vs    346.0</p>
<p>    Direct costs of sales	 6,158.4	  vs  2,940.1</p>
<p>    Indirect costs of sales     1,167.3	  vs    916.3</p>
<p>    Other expenditures		326.9	  vs    346.9</p>
<p>    Financial activities' profit  108.4	  vs    316.3</p>
<p>    Extraordinary result	    374.7 profit vs    248.2 loss</p>
<p>NOTE - The figures are consolidated and were calculated</p>
<p>according to the Hungarian accounting standard. The figures for</p>
<p>1996 are unaudited. Novotrade Rt is a holding company.</p>
<p>Novotrade, as a result of winning a lawsuit against Magyar</p>
<p>Kulkereskedelmi Bank, added 279 million forints, accounted for</p>
<p>as extraordinary expenditure in 1995, to its extraordinary</p>
<p>revenues in 1996, the company said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
